# Service-account key files. These are private keys: a single `git add -A`
# is all it takes to publish one, and revoking a leaked key means rotating
# every consumer of it. Generated keys belong outside the repo entirely —
# this pattern is a backstop, not a licence to keep them here.
*-key.json
**/service-account*.json
